/**
 * Shared machinery for DOM-backed text on the web-native backend.
 *
 * A text/tex mobject on the browser path is a plain {@link VMobject}-compatible
 * bounding box carrying a {@link NativeTextPayload}; the geometry is measured
 * (KaTeX for math, the browser text engine for text) and the content lives in
 * the payload HTML.  {@link NativeTextBox} is the box class, and
 * {@link applyNativeSeed} attaches payloads whose `color` and `fontHeightUnits`
 * are derived from the mobject at render time:
 *
 *  - `color` follows `mobject.get_color()`, so `set_color` /
 *    `set_color_by_gradient` / `set_color_by_tex` keep working on a payload
 *    that was snapshotted at construction time.
 *  - `fontHeightUnits` is recomputed from the box height, so `scale()` and
 *    `font_size` keep working (a fixed font size would not follow the box).
 *
 * Payloads live in a `WeakMap`, which a mobject copy cannot see, so both box
 * classes re-attach their payload in `copy_with_seen` / `__deepcopy__`.
 */
